Add decompression bomb check to GdImageFile (CVE-2026-55380)

GdImageFile._open() read the image dimensions from the GD header and built
the raw decoder tile without ever validating the resulting image size. A
crafted .gd file declaring huge width/height would allocate an enormous
image, enabling a decompression-bomb denial of service. Add the same
Image._decompression_bomb_check(self.size) guard used by other plugins,
right after the size is parsed.

