CVE-2026-59204: The JPEG2000 decoder declared total_component_width once
outside the per-tile decode loop, so its accumulator was never reset between
tiles. A crafted multi-tile JPEG2000 file could grow this value unboundedly,
defeating the tile_bytes overflow guard and causing excessive memory
allocation (CWE-770). Scope the accumulator to each tile so the overflow
check is evaluated per tile.

Upstream fix: 13ada41172142f2fd9f0906f615a00ea623a11ca (PR #9704)

